WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.980
Good morning John!

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:05.560
And pre-congratulations on your your little wiggly sticky baby thing. Any day now, still waiting!

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.220
Also, thank you for providing me with several impossible tasks to acomplish while you're

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.400
busy relaxing on your paternity leave.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.420
Living all day reading pretentious novels in the sunshine, eating fancy waffles...

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.240
I don't have a lot of data on how exactly to take care of a newborn child, but I figured something like that

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.960
So yeah! I'm happy to fix all the worlds problems while you're busy cuddling with your new baby in well rested luxury.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.889
Speaking of all the world's problems a few weeks ago I made a video that

00:00:28.889 --> 00:00:33.229
highlighted some of the pretty dramatic changes that humanity has ennacted upon the earth.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.340
I made a video because I wanted to give people a more complete picture on how we impact our planet

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:43.340
and maybe inspire some people to help! And in that,  I think that video miserably failed.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.070
It was overwhelming, it made people hate themselves for being a part of humanity

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.062
and it was paralyzing more than inspiring.

00:00:49.062 --> 00:00:52.083
Our brains are just not good at understanding this sort of thing, for example

00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:56.203
we way overestimate our abilty to deal with stuff that we control

00:00:56.203 --> 00:01:00.472
like I think I can run five busineses and occasionally jump over to Seatle

00:01:00.472 --> 00:01:03.112
to help kickstart a space telescope. No problem! I can deal with all that! No, I won't go crazy!

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.920
But we way underestimate our ability as a species to affect stuff that we feel like we can't control individually.

00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:14.486
And we have a know cognitive bias on remembering and basing our decisions on negative experiences

00:01:14.486 --> 00:01:18.366
and not on the positive ones like we have to have like ten positive experiences to weigh out every negative one.

00:01:18.366 --> 00:01:24.406
What I'm trying to say is that you are being lied to by your own brain and also by you know, society and fox news

00:01:24.406 --> 00:01:26.260
and to some extent me in that video I made.

00:01:26.264 --> 00:01:30.444
Humanity is not a cancer! Deforestation happens because people wanna provide better lives

00:01:30.444 --> 00:01:35.560
for themselves and for their families. Rivers run dry because we're irrigating crops so that children don't starve

00:01:35.568 --> 00:01:39.553
The amazing thing for me is that humans are constantly solving these huge problems

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.840
and we never notice that we do and we never celebrate!

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.640
Disasters happen all at once! Sucesses happen slowly and gradually

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.034
and they are interrupted by disasters, but they continue despite them!

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:57.495
This is a graph of the health and wealth of every contry in the world from 1900 to 2011.

00:01:57.495 --> 00:02:04.274
Every country is better off. In fact, some contries in Africa are doing better now than the United States was in 1900

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.620
Here is what I think happens: I think that we look at a graph and the graph shows something increasing

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:13.920
wether that is climate change, or oil use, or deforestation and there is a disaster point somewhere

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.200
at the top and that graph is gonna get there maybe in ten years and we think:

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.380
We have ten years left to live on the earth!

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:24.140
But usually, we adapt! And capitalism adapts!

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.100
And technology adapts, and my god, even congress adapts!

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:32.840
We consistently every single year avoid the apocalypse not because there is one

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.140
single superhero. This isn't a television drama!

00:02:36.143 --> 00:02:38.121
But because we do things together!

00:02:38.121 --> 00:02:44.381
We do these things as activists and chemists and engineers and physicists and poets and songwriters.

00:02:44.381 --> 00:02:47.461
And writers and politicians, and even bureaucrats.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.985
We are the superhero!

00:02:48.985 --> 00:02:51.432
None of us individually, but all of us together.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.880
My trip to Seatle to the museum of flight

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:58.280
to help planetary resources launch their space telescope kickstarter was inspiring, unsurprisingly,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.196
but maybe for surprising reasons. Wasn't just, you know,

00:03:01.196 --> 00:03:04.188
people are going to band together and crowdfund a freaking space telescope.

00:03:04.188 --> 00:03:08.761
but also, it was seeing artifacts of great projects that humanity has enacted together

00:03:08.761 --> 00:03:12.730
and meeting people who are extremely smart and dedicated people who are

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.640
working their butts of to make sure that humanity continues its path towards a

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.130
more prosperous future to the majority of people the majority of the time.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.140
And it's not just those supersmart people. It's all of us!

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.840
All of us working together to make the world work!

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.480
It turns out that they're very good at solving problems, but they do not solve themselves.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.880
To what I've realised is that working hard to create a better future does not come from a place

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:39.180
of wanting to avoid inevitable apocalypse, but instead it comes from a place of optimism.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:44.380
And it turns out that somehow there are a tremendous number of things to be optimistic about

00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:45.406
and that's pretty great!

00:03:45.406 --> 00:03:52.006
John, I'll see you or potentially someone else, if you have a baby, on Tuesday!

